.TH HARNESS 1 "2026-07-19" "AI Harness" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
harness \- AI coding harness \(em agentic CLI for local and remote LLMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B harness
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B harness
is an agentic coding assistant that runs in your terminal. It connects to any
OpenAI-compatible API \(em including local models via Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM,
remote providers like OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, and others \(em and
provides tools for reading, writing, editing files, running shell commands,
and searching the web.
.PP
The harness operates in three modes:
.IP \(bu 3
\fBInteractive REPL\fR (default): type prompts, get responses, use slash commands
.IP \(bu
\fBPrint mode\fR (\fB\-p\fR/\fB\-\-prompt\fR): run a single prompt and print the response
.IP \(bu
\fBTUI mode\fR (\fB\&tui\fR): blessed-contrib terminal UI for multi-session management
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Model Settings
.TP
.BI \-m " <name>" , \-\-model " <name>"
Select a model by key from the
.B [model.<name>]
sections in config.toml.
Defaults to the model set in
.BR [models] " " default .
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " <0\-2>"
Override the sampling temperature for this session.
When unset, the model uses its own default.
.TP
.BI \-\-top\-p " <0\-1>"
Override top_p (nucleus sampling) for this session.
When unset, the model uses its own default.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " <int>"
Override the random seed for deterministic sampling.
When unset, no seed is sent and the model samples nondeterministically.
.TP
.BR \-\-drop\-params ", " \-\-no\-drop\-params
Strip unsupported parameters automatically
(e.g. temperature on reasoning models like OpenAI o-series,
DeepSeek Reasoner, or models running on older local servers).
See
.B drop_params_extra
in
.BR [model.<name>]
to extend the stripped-param list per model.
.SS Output and Display
.TP
.BI \-w " <cols>" , \-\-width " <cols>"
Set the output wrap width in columns (minimum 20, default 80).
.TP
.BR \-\-styled ", " \-\-no\-styled
Enable or disable styled Markdown rendering.
Styled mode buffers the full response, renders it, and writes it
on completion. Unstyled mode streams tokens as they arrive.
Auto-detected from config and
.B HARNESS_STYLED
env var; defaults to unstyled.
.TP
.BR \-\-plan ", " \-\-build
Start in plan mode (read-only, no modifications) or build mode
(modifications allowed). Build mode is the default.
.TP
.BR \-\-hide\-thinking ", " \-\-hide\-tools
Suppress thinking text display or tool call indicator lines.
.TP
.B \-\-ansi\-256
Force ANSI 256-color mode, disabling truecolor detection.
.TP
.BR \-\-status\-line ", " \-\-no\-status\-line
Show or hide the progress spinner during model thinking.
Defaults to enabled.
.SS Session Management
.TP
.BI \-S " <id>" , \-\-session " <id>"
Resume a specific session by its ID
(e.g.
.BR 20250719\-142300\-a1b2 ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-resume
Resume the most recent INTERACTIVE session.
.TP
.B \-\-sessions
List all saved sessions with their IDs, labels, message counts,
and timestamps.
.TP
.B \-\-purge\-empty\-sessions
Remove session files that contain no messages (empty sessions).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Preview what \-\-purge\-empty\-sessions would delete without
actually deleting.
.SS Agent & Pipeline
.TP
.BI \-\-agent " <name>"
Load an agent definition or pipeline from
.BR .harness/agents/<name>.toml
or
.BR .harness/pipelines/<name>.toml .
Agent definitions can set a custom system prompt, tools, mode,
and temperature. Pipelines execute a sequence of agents.
If the flag is given without a value, the harness lists available
agents and pipelines and exits.
.SS Context Management
.TP
.BR \-\-context\-management ", " \-\-no\-context\-management
Enable or disable automatic context truncation and compaction.
When enabled, the harness drops older messages and/or summarizes
them when the conversation exceeds the usable context window.
Defaults to enabled.
.SS Theming
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " <name>"
Apply a bundled color theme. Available themes:
github, matrix, opencode, dracula, tokyonight, monokai,
nightowl, flexoki, carbonfox, aura, vesper, vercel,
catppuccin, synthwave84.
Can also be configured permanently via the
.B [theme]
section in config.toml with a
.B file
key.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
List all available bundled theme names and exit.
.SS Miscellaneous
.TP
.BI \-p " <text>" , \-\-prompt " <text>"
Run a single prompt in print mode and exit.
.TP
.BI \-s " <provider>" , \-\-search " <provider>"
Set the search provider.
Valid providers:
.BR tavily ,
.BR duckduckgo ,
.BR exa .
If the flag is given without a value, the harness lists available
providers and exits.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-iterations " <n>"
Override the maximum number of agent iterations per prompt.
Use 0 for unlimited iterations. Default is 25.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Enable file-based logging to
.BR ~/.harness/logs/<session\-id>.jsonl .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display this help message and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B model
List configured models. Shows name, display name, kind, key status,
and base URL. The default model is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.B sessions
List saved sessions (same as
.BR \-\-sessions ).
.TP
.B config
Show the effective configuration: config file paths, default model,
permission mode, search provider, and MCP server count.
.TP
.B init
Create the default configuration at
.BR ~/.harness/config.toml ,
a
.B .env
template at
.BR ~/.harness/.env ,
and optionally an
.B AGENTS.md
file for the current project.
.TP
.BI "skill " <sub> " [" name ]
Manage skills.
.I sub
is one of:
.RS
.TP
.B list
List available skills and their enabled status.
.TP
.BI enable " <name>"
Enable a skill by adding a hint to AGENTS.md.
.TP
.BI disable " <name>"
Disable a skill by removing its hint from AGENTS.md.
.RE
.TP
.B tui
Launch the blessed-contrib Terminal UI for multi-session management.
Applies the same flag overrides as interactive mode
.RB ( \-\-temperature ,
.BR \-\-top\-p ,
.BR \-\-seed ,
.BR \-\-drop\-params ,
.BR \-\-context\-management ,
etc.).
.SH INTERACTIVE SLASH COMMANDS
The following commands are available inside the interactive REPL:
.TP
.B /help
Show the list of available slash commands.
.TP
.B /search
Show the current search provider.
.TP
.BI "/search " <provider>
Switch search provider
.RB ( tavily ", " duckduckgo ", " exa ).
.TP
.B /key
Show usage for setting temporary API keys.
.TP
.BI "/key " <ENV_VAR>
Set an environment variable (e.g. an API key) for the current session.
Prompts for the value without echoing.
.TP
.B /temperature
Show the current temperature setting.
.TP
.BI "/temperature " <0\-2>
Set the temperature for the current session.
.TP
.B /agent
Show the current agent name and description.
.TP
.BI "/agent " <name>
Switch to a named agent or pipeline. Lists available options
if called without arguments.
.TP
.B /session
Show current session info: ID, model, search provider, temperature,
message count, creation and last-save timestamps.
.TP
.B /sessions
List all saved sessions (same as
.BR \-\-sessions ).
.TP
.BI "/resume " [<id>]
Resume the most recent session (no argument) or a specific session by ID.
.TP
.BR /exit ", " /quit
Save the current session and exit.
.TP
.B "Ctrl+C, Ctrl+D"
Save the current session and exit.
.TP
.B !<command>
Run a shell command directly without going through the agent.
Uses the same shell as the agent (bash, PowerShell, cmd.exe).
.TP
.B /plan
Switch to plan mode (read-only, no modifications).
.TP
.B /build
Switch to build mode (modifications allowed, default).
.TP
.B /hide-thinking
Suppress thinking text display.
.TP
.B /show-thinking
Show thinking text (re-enable after /hide-thinking).
.TP
.B /hide-tools
Hide tool call indicator lines.
.TP
.B /show-tools
Show tool call indicator lines (re-enable after /hide-tools).
.TP
.BI "/export " [txt|file]
Export the current session as .md (default) or .txt.
.TP
.B /summarize
Write a session summary to the project's memory-bank/.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is written in TOML format. Files are loaded in order:
global first, then project files walking up from the working directory.
Later files override earlier ones.
.SS Model Definition
.RS
.nf
[model.<name>]
model       = "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"   # Required: model identifier
kind        = "openai-compatible"             # Required: provider kind
base_url    = "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"  # API endpoint
api_key     = "sk-..."                        # Inline API key (less secure)
api_key_env = "OPENROUTER_API_KEY"            # Env var holding the key
name        = "DeepSeek V4 Flash"             # Human-readable display name
max_tokens  = 4096                            # Max response tokens
temperature = 0.7                             # Sampling temperature (0\(en2)
top_p       = 0.9                             # Nucleus sampling (0\(en1)
seed        = 42                              # Deterministic seed
stop        = ["\\n\\n"]                      # Stop sequences
drop_params = true                            # Auto-strip unsupported params
drop_params_extra = ["stream_options"]        # Extra params to always strip
.RE
.SS Models Table
.RS
.nf
[models]
default = "deepseek"
.RE
.SS MCP Servers
.RS
.nf
[mcp_servers.<name>]
command = "npx"
args    = ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "."]
env     = { KEY = "value" }
.RE
.SS Permissions
.RS
.nf
[permissions]
mode = "ask"  # auto | ask | accept-edits | deny

[permissions.tools]
bash       = "ask"
write      = "ask"
read       = "auto"
edit       = "auto"
web_search = "ask"
web_fetch  = "ask"
.RE
.SS Search
.RS
.nf
[search]
provider = "tavily"  # tavily | duckduckgo | exa
.RE
.SS CLI
.RS
.nf
[cli]
styled      = false  # Enable styled Markdown by default
status_line = true   # Show progress spinner
.RE
.SS Context
.RS
.nf
[context]
management      = true   # Enable context truncation/compaction
window          = 32768  # Context window in tokens
response_budget = 4096   # Tokens reserved for model response
.RE
.SS Formatting
.RS
.nf
[format]
on_write = true
tools = { "*.py" = "ruff format", "*.{js,ts}" = "prettier --write" }
.RE
.SS Theme
.RS
.nf
[theme]
colors = { error = "#ff4444", success = "#44ff44" }
.RE
.SS Compactification
.RS
.nf
[compactification]
model       = "qwen3.5:latest"
base_url    = "http://localhost:11434/v1"
kind        = "openai-compatible"
api_key_env = "OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
.RE
.PP
The compactification section defines an optional separate model used
for summarizing older conversation history. When unset, the main model
is used for summarization.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.harness/config.toml
Global user configuration file.
.TP
.B <project>/.harness/config.toml
Per-project configuration (searched upward from CWD).
.TP
.B ~/.harness/sessions/
Directory containing session JSON files. Each file records the
conversation history, model, search provider, and timestamps.
.TP
.B ~/.harness/.env
User-level environment variables (loaded before project .env).
.TP
.B <cwd>/.env
Project-level environment variables (override user .env).
Shell env vars take precedence over both.
.TP
.B ~/.harness/drop_params_cache.json
Cache of parameter restrictions discovered per model. Prevents
repeated API errors when a model rejects certain parameters.
.TP
.B <project>/AGENTS.md
Project rules file appended to the system prompt. Also contains
skill activation hints (\fB<!-- @harness skill:<name> -->\fR).
.TP
.B <project>/CLAUDE.md
Fallback project rules if AGENTS.md is not found.
.TP
.B ~/.config/harness/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
Global skill definitions.
.TP
.B <project>/.harness/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
Project-level skill definitions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.SS Display/Behavior
.TP
.B HARNESS_STYLED
Set to
.B true
or
.B 1
to enable styled Markdown output;
.B false
or
.B 0
to disable. Overridden by
.BR \-\-styled "/" \-\-no-styled .
.TP
.B HARNESS_CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT
Set to
.B true
or
.B 1
to enable context management;
.B false
or
.B 0
to disable. Overridden by
.BR \-\-context-management "/" \-\-no-context-management .
.TP
.B HARNESS_STATUS_LINE
Set to
.B true
or
.B 1
to show the progress spinner;
.B false
or
.B 0
to hide. Overridden by
.BR \-\-status-line "/" \-\-no-status-line .
.TP
.B HARNESS_HIDE_THINKING
Set to
.B true
or
.B 1
to hide thinking text by default.
.TP
.B HARNESS_HIDE_TOOLS
Set to
.B true
or
.B 1
to hide tool call indicator lines by default.
.TP
.B HARNESS_FORCE_256_COLOR
Set to
.B 1
to force ANSI 256-color mode (disables truecolor).
Unset or
.B 0
means auto-detect. Overridden by
.BR \-\-ansi\-256 .
.TP
.B HARNESS_MAX_ITERATIONS
Override the maximum number of agent iterations per prompt.
Default is 25. Overridden by
.BR \-\-max\-iterations .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to any value to disable all color output. Overrides
.B CLICOLOR
and color capability detection.
.TP
.B CLICOLOR
Set to
.B 0
to disable color output.
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
Set to any value to force color output (bypasses
.BR NO_COLOR ).
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Color capability hint (e.g.
.BR truecolor ,
.BR 256color ).
Auto-detected from terminal.
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal type identifier. Used for color capability detection.
.SS Model API Keys
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
API key for OpenRouter (also used for OpenRouter search).
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
API key for OpenAI.
.TP
.B DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
API key for DeepSeek.
.TP
.B XAI_API_KEY
API key for xAI.
.TP
.B GROQ_API_KEY
API key for Groq.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
API key for Anthropic.
.PP
Any model can alternatively use a custom env var via
.B api_key_env
in its config section.
.SS Search Providers
.TP
.B TAVILY_API_KEY
API key for Tavily search.
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_SEARCH_MODEL
Model identifier to use for OpenRouter-powered search.
Defaults to
.BR deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash .
.PP
DuckDuckGo search is free and requires no API key.
.TP
.B EXA_API_KEY
API key for Exa search provider.
.SS Shell
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell to use for the bash tool on non-Windows systems.
Defaults to
.BR /bin/sh .
.TP
.B COMSPEC
Shell to use for the bash tool on Windows.
Defaults to
.BR cmd.exe .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (help displayed, prompt completed, or clean exit).
.TP
1
General error (invalid config, unknown command, model validation
failure, or runtime error).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start interactive mode:
.B harness
.TP
Run a single prompt with a specific model:
.B "harness \-m deepseek \-p \(dqExplain monads\(dq"
.TP
Start with a different temperature:
.B "harness \-\-temperature 0.8"
.TP
Use a deterministic seed for reproducibility:
.B "harness \-\-seed 42 \-\-top-p 1"
.TP
Resume the most recent session:
.B "harness \-r"
.TP
Resume a specific session:
.B "harness \-S 20250719\-142300\-a1b2"
.TP
Use DuckDuckGo for search (no API key needed):
.B "harness \-\-search duckduckgo"
.TP
Disable context management for a session:
.B "harness \-\-no-context-management"
.TP
Enable styled Markdown output:
.B "harness \-\-styled"
.TP
List configured models:
.B "harness model"
.TP
Show effective configuration:
.B "harness config"
.TP
Initialize configuration:
.B "harness init"
.TP
Launch TUI mode:
.B "harness tui"
.TP
Disable automatic parameter stripping:
.B "harness \-\-no-drop-params"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR tmux (1)
.PP
